==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[The Face]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 5.33~12 seconds<sup>160f~360f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 5.33~12 seconds<sup>160f~360f</sup>.
**4 [[Tackey]]s spawn, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Mooth]] spawns.
**1 [[Mooth]] spawns.
**2 [[Shy Boy]]s spawn, delay 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
**2 [[Shy Boy]]s spawn, delay 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is very easy in comparison to [[Lord's Lecture]]. Since the main threats don't spawn until the enemy base is hit, you can stall the Doges in the beginning using a meatshield with high health but low damage, like [[Manic Eraser Cat]] (or [[Li'l Eraser Cat]] in 4-crown), after which you will have ample money before hitting the base. Once you hit the base, you need to constantly keep up the pressure against the enemies, as letting the Tackeys stack up is a recipe for disaster. Units such as [[Can Can Cat]], [[Fishman Cat]], [[Courier Cat]], and [[Cameraman Cat]] are recommended as they have great matchups against the Shy Boys, who are the main pushers in this stage, and The Face, who acts as a wall preventing your units from being able to hit the Tackeys. Once The Face is dead, you can spawn a rusher unit like [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to clean up the stage rapidly.

==Trivia==
*Based on its Japanese name, Batabata Daikokubashira (バタバタ大黒柱, "Clattering Central Pillar"), the [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark Enemies]] in Cracked Column may be a reference to how 大黒柱 ''daikokubashira'' (the central pillar that holds up a traditional Japanese house; a mainstay; the provider/breadwinner of a household) contains the kanji for black (黒).

